  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1410.06 Certification Prior to Shipment of Off-Specification Used Oil",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1410.06 Certification Prior to Shipment of Off-Specification Used Oil.\n\n(a) Before a used oil marketer directs the first shipment of off-specification used oil fuel to a used oil burner, they shall obtain a one-time written and signed notice from the used oil burner certifying that the used oil burner:\n\n(1) Has submitted notification of the burner’s used oil management activities to the department, or if out of state, to the state or EPA region in which the burner is located; and\n\n(2) Will burn the off-specification used oil only in an industrial furnace or boiler identified in Env-Hw 1409.03(a).\n\n(b) Certifications described in (a), above, shall be kept as specified in Env-Hw 1410.07(a)(3).\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
